Coverage Goals:
- Aim for 80-90% coverage (100% is often impractical)
- Focus on critical business logic
- Low coverage indicates gaps
- High coverage doesn't mean good tests

Coverage Anti-patterns:
- Testing trivial code to increase coverage
- Removing code to improve coverage
- Writing tests that assert nothing
- Ignoring coverage for error paths

